// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_cmdl32_arbitrary_file_download.yml
// ID Sigma: f37aba28-a9e6-4045-882c-d5004043b337
// Título: Potential Arbitrary File Download Via Cmdl32.EXE
// Descripción: Detects execution of Cmdl32 with the "/vpn" and "/lan" flags.
Attackers can abuse this utility in order to download arbitrary files via a configuration file.
Inspect the location and the content of the file passed as an argument in order to determine if it is suspicious.

// Fecha de creación: 2021-11-03
// Fecha de modificación: 2024-04-22
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: medium
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_cmdl32_arbitrary_file_download.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\cmdl32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "CMDL32.EXE") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "/vpn" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/lan")
